review_comments.body:
Hi @sobolevn I doubt the possibility of replicating this without monkeypatching. The issue stems from, during a mixed format buffer comparison, `memory_richcompare` function calls a re-entrant `struct.Struct.unpack_from` that is loaded by a `PyImport_ImportModuleAttrString("struct", "Struct")` call in the [struct_get_unpacker](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/9609574e7fd36edfaa8b575558a82cc14e65bfbc/Objects/memoryobject.c#L2079). Is there anyway you would recommend to work around it ?
```c
/* Return a new unpacker for the given format. */
static struct unpacker *
struct_get_unpacker(const char *fmt, Py_ssize_t itemsize)
{
    ...

    // struct.Struct Importation
    Struct = PyImport_ImportModuleAttrString("struct", "Struct");
    if (Struct == NULL)
        return NULL;

    x = unpacker_new();

    ...

    x->unpack_from = PyObject_GetAttrString(structobj, "unpack_from");
    if (x->unpack_from == NULL)
        goto error;
    ...

}
```

